meta {
  name: solve_ik (fixture pose)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/mcp
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 6,
    "method": "tools/call",
    "params": {
      "name": "solve_ik",
      "arguments": {
        "arm": "{{arm}}",
        "frame": "arm1_base",
        "pose": {
          "x": {{pose_x}},
          "y": {{pose_y}},
          "z": {{pose_z}},
          "qx": {{pose_qx}},
          "qy": {{pose_qy}},
          "qz": {{pose_qz}},
          "qw": {{pose_qw}}
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Report only: it never writes. To get ok=true, fill pose_* in the environment with a pose produced by
  tools/ik_pose_fixture.py (forward kinematics from the arm's current angles), so the solver has to come back
  to where the arm already is: expect ok true, pos_err ~0.0 mm, about 7 iterations.

  Needs the IK node up (arm1_ik / arm2_ik) and the supervisor running: the supervisor waits up to 5 s for the
  correlated answer and nothing is written on the report path either way.
}
